WEBVTT

00:00:01.710 --> 00:00:10.169
Last week on How We Made Your Mother, I always kind of felt that that my performance annoyed you, Josh.
上周在《我们如何造就你的母亲》节目中，我总觉得我的表现惹恼了你，乔什。

00:00:10.169 --> 00:00:10.669
What?
什么？

00:00:10.580 --> 00:00:31.850
I'm alone, be I won't be soon, in New York City, when I see you, please permit me to tell you everything in New York City.
我独自一人在纽约，虽然不会很快，当我见到你时，请允许我告诉你在纽约的一切。

00:00:31.850 --> 00:00:32.850
Tell me more.
告诉我更多。

00:00:32.850 --> 00:00:33.850
Tell me more.
告诉我更多。

00:00:33.850 --> 00:00:49.159
Because, honestly, because of the, like, more because of this conversation that we're having because I was literally, I was rarely at work, um, too cognitive, as laser focused as I was of like the comedy turns and like doing that stuff.
因为，老实说，因为，更多的是因为我们正在进行的这次谈话，因为我真的，我很少在工作，嗯，太认知，像激光一样专注，就像喜剧转弯一样，喜欢做那些事情。

00:00:49.159 --> 00:00:54.759
I was very indifferent to the heart and the pathos of it because I wasn't good in that way.
我对内心及其悲痛非常漠不关心，因为我在这方面并不擅长。

00:00:54.759 --> 00:00:58.560
And I know that that was your job, right?
我知道那是你的工作，对吗？

00:00:58.560 --> 00:01:16.159
And so I remember often days when we were filming and I sent sort of frustration from you because like you wanted the scene to be like a good scene and I was looking at you like, I'm doing spitttakes.
所以我记得很多时候，当我们拍摄时，我会从你那里发出一些沮丧的声音，因为就像你希望场景像一个好的场景一样，而我看着你，就像我在吐痰一样。

00:01:16.159 --> 00:01:22.359
Like, we're on this weird sitcom between two things.
就像，我们正在观看一部介于两件事之间的奇怪情景喜剧。

00:01:22.359 --> 00:01:25.359
So, and it wasn't like, I thought, I agree with that.
所以，我想，我并不同意这一点。

00:01:25.359 --> 00:01:26.560
I guess this is my point.
我想这就是我的观点。

00:01:26.560 --> 00:01:28.959
Like, I'm not like airing Dirty Laundry or anything.
就像，我不喜欢播放脏衣服之类的东西。

00:01:28.959 --> 00:01:36.640
I'm just saying, I think it required the two, like multiple perspectives of all of us to create it.
我只是说，我认为它需要我们所有人的两个人的多重视角来创造它。

00:01:36.640 --> 00:01:47.180
But as it was happening, I was sort of like, I think that Josh is just kind of annoyed by the, Do you know what I think it flying around all the time, just like doing bits?
但当它发生时，我有点像，我认为乔什只是有点恼火，你知道我认为它一直飞来飞去，就像做点什么吗？

00:01:47.180 --> 00:01:53.260
I think it might have been a little bit like of confusion between actor and character.
我认为这可能有点像演员和角色之间的混淆。

00:01:53.260 --> 00:01:58.260
Like Barney was often incredibly almost dismissive of Ted.
就像巴尼经常对泰德表现出令人难以置信的近乎不屑一顾的态度。

00:01:58.579 --> 00:02:06.859
Like, and you were so good at playing that, that I think sometimes like I felt dismissed by Neil, but I was being dismissed by Barney.
就像，你非常擅长玩这个，我想有时我感觉自己被尼尔解雇了，但我却被巴尼解雇了。

00:02:06.859 --> 00:02:07.700
Do you know what I'm saying?
你知道我在说什么吗？

00:02:07.700 --> 00:02:08.539
Yeah.
是的。

00:02:08.539 --> 00:02:15.180
Like, you know when your body can't tell the difference, even though your mind is the difference?
就像，你知道什么时候你的身体无法分辨出差异，即使你的思想是差异？

00:02:15.180 --> 00:02:22.340
And I think there was, but when I look back on it, I'm so delighted by our weird chemistry.
我想是有的，但当我回想起来时，我对我们奇怪的化学反应感到非常高兴。

00:02:22.340 --> 00:02:23.340
It is chemistry.
这是化学。

00:02:23.340 --> 00:02:24.180
That chemistry.
那种化学反应。

00:02:24.180 --> 00:02:31.620
I think that there was something in that kind of tension that you're describing that would come out sideways a little bit sometimes.
我认为你所描述的那种紧张气氛有时会出现一些偏差。

00:02:31.620 --> 00:02:35.219
That was actually the secret sauce in making that make sense.
这实际上是让它有意义的秘诀。

00:02:35.219 --> 00:02:37.500
I never- I 100% agree to.
我从来没有——我百分百同意。

00:02:37.500 --> 00:02:41.219
I never doubt that Barney is obsessed with Ted.
我从不怀疑巴尼对泰德很着迷。

00:02:41.219 --> 00:02:44.219
And I never doubt that he wants the best for him.
我从不怀疑他想要给他最好的。

00:02:44.219 --> 00:02:52.939
And also, sometimes, oftentimes, they're on totally different pages, like in terms of like where their heads are, what they're looking to do, whether.
而且，有时，很多时候，他们处于完全不同的页面，比如他们的头在哪里，他们想要做什么，是否。

00:02:52.939 --> 00:02:59.860
So there was always some resistance that I had to play in a lot of scenes with you.
所以在很多场景中我必须和你一起扮演一些阻力。

00:02:59.860 --> 00:03:05.379
And it's true, we were like inhabiting different worlds, but they were all under this larger umbrella world.
确实，我们就像居住在不同的世界，但它们都在这个更大的保护伞世界之下。

00:03:05.379 --> 00:03:06.219
It's totally true.
这是完全正确的。

00:03:06.219 --> 00:03:12.979
But I think you're right, but I don't think it was, I think it was something that worked beautifully for the show.
但我认为你是对的，但我不认为是这样，我认为这对演出来说非常有效。

00:03:12.979 --> 00:03:13.819
All right.
好的。

00:03:13.819 --> 00:03:26.340
I concur, it's nice to have these conversations now because while it was happening, it felt to me some like a disconnect and when you explain it that way, it makes perfect sense.
我同意，现在进行这些对话很好，因为当它发生时，我感觉有些脱节，当你这样解释时，它就完全有道理了。

00:03:26.340 --> 00:03:28.620
It's not like an unresolved issue that I have or anything.
这不像是我遇到的未解决的问题或任何事情。

00:03:28.620 --> 00:03:46.849
I just remember like being at craft service or something And it was, and you were personally just more like buddy, buddy with Jason and that we'd like say, hey to each other or whatever, but like we were sort of doing different shows.
我只记得像在工艺品服务或其他什么地方，而且你个人更像是朋友，与杰森的朋友，我们想说，互相问候或其他什么，但就像我们在做不同的节目一样。

00:03:46.849 --> 00:03:49.330
And when it was, we were filming it.
当它发生时，我们正在拍摄它。

00:03:49.330 --> 00:03:54.650
And I would think like, it's just mad at me, everything is just mad at me a lot.
我会想，它只是生我的气，一切都对我很生气。

00:03:54.650 --> 00:03:56.729
Like, am I doing something to annoy him?
比如，我做了什么让他生气的事吗？

00:03:56.729 --> 00:04:22.970
I would like to relieve you of some of this by saying, one is what I just described, But two, I think that when the show came on, I remember like early, like, remember we did that photo shoot for People Magazine where we were all kind of like arranged in different, like you and Ali and Jason had had, that you'd been to up front, you'd had shows on the air, people would recognize you from different things.
我想通过这样的话来减轻你的负担，一是我刚才所描述的，但是二，我认为当节目开始时，我记得很早就，记得我们为《人物》杂志拍了那张照片，我们都被安排在不同的位置，就像你和阿里和杰森一样，你在前面，你在广播中播出过节目，人们会从不同的事物中认出你。

00:04:22.970 --> 00:04:31.170
Me and Kobe, Kobe, I think like, was a little to the man or boy, and like she was just like, kind of was like pretty, she's just comfortable.
我和科比，科比，我想，有点像男人或男孩，就像她一样，有点漂亮，她很舒服。

00:04:31.170 --> 00:04:34.470
There was something about, you know, I had been on Broadway.
你知道，我曾在百老汇演出过。

00:04:34.470 --> 00:04:36.069
This was like my fourth pilot.
这就像我的第四位飞行员。

00:04:36.069 --> 00:04:38.670
I was not a famous person, you know?
我本来就不是什么名人，你知道吗？

00:04:38.670 --> 00:04:47.069
And I think that I had a harder adjustment with like losing my anonymity, being the center of this show.
我认为我经历了更艰难的调整，比如失去匿名性，成为这个节目的中心。

00:04:47.069 --> 00:04:48.430
I think it was hard for me.
我认为这对我来说很难。

00:04:48.430 --> 00:05:00.750
And I felt that you and Allie and Jason, especially were like so much more comfortable with the camera, so much more comfortable with like being recognized in the weird ways your life changes when you get on a show like this.
我觉得你、艾莉和杰森，尤其是对镜头感到更加自在，当你参加这样的节目时，你的生活会以奇怪的方式被认可，这让你更加自在。

00:05:00.750 --> 00:05:04.949
And I think I just, sometimes I, you know, I kept running to the jungle and doing ayahuasca.
我想我只是，有时我，你知道，我一直跑到丛林里做死藤水。

00:05:04.949 --> 00:05:14.790
Like I didn't know, I didn't know how to process this in a way that felt healthy other than kind of like trying to, I don't know, keep it at arm's length.
就像我不知道一样，我不知道如何以一种感觉健康的方式来处理这个问题，而不是试图，我不知道，与它保持一定的距离。

00:05:14.790 --> 00:05:19.550
And I guess, like if I was like a little pissy or something, I'm sorry.
我想，如果我有点小气什么的，我很抱歉。

00:05:19.550 --> 00:05:25.550
Like I think that I was just trying to manage a lot of different things and emotions and they came outside ways sometimes.
就像我认为我只是想管理很多不同的事情和情绪，有时它们会以某种方式出现。

00:05:25.550 --> 00:05:27.430
I totally hear you and I totally appreciate that.
我完全听到了你的意见，我非常感激。

00:05:27.430 --> 00:05:29.509
And that makes perfect sense.
这是完全有道理的。

00:05:29.509 --> 00:05:48.959
And I don't think there was a singular thing because we were being asked for almost a decade every day to be like remembering lines, like doing physical comedy, doing heartfelt monologues, what's seen as next, what's happening in my personal life.
我不认为有什么奇怪的事情，因为近十年来我们每天都被要求记住台词，比如做肢体喜剧，做发自内心的独白，接下来会发生什么，我的个人生活中会发生什么。

00:05:48.959 --> 00:05:50.800
Like there's so much that was going on all the time.
好像一直有很多事情在发生。

00:05:50.800 --> 00:05:56.160
You guys were all having kids, like which I now understand is the biggest change your life can ever undergo.
你们都已经有了孩子，我现在明白这是你们生活中能经历的最大的改变。

00:05:56.160 --> 00:06:06.399
But also, Neil, you know, I don't know we've even talked about, I think we talked about this, but like Neil and I did this John Robin Bates play like months before we got cast as Ted and Barney.
而且，尼尔，你知道，我不知道我们甚至讨论过，我想我们讨论过这个，但是就像尼尔和我在我们扮演泰德和巴尼之前几个月就演了这部约翰·罗宾·贝茨的戏一样。

00:06:06.399 --> 00:06:12.000
We played lovers in this play called The Paris Letter, a great play and we had a great experience doing it.
我们在这部名为《巴黎的信》的戏剧中扮演恋人，这是一部很棒的戏剧，我们演得很开心。

00:06:12.000 --> 00:06:19.079
And I think there was also like this strange change between like we were doing this very intense intimate theater piece.
我认为我们之间也存在这种奇怪的变化，就像我们正在做一部非常激烈的亲密戏剧作品一样。

00:06:19.079 --> 00:06:22.720
And then suddenly we were Ted and Barney, like literally like four months later.
然后突然我们就变成了泰德和巴尼，就像四个月后一样。

00:06:22.720 --> 00:06:26.639
And it was like, it was like, it gave me vertigo, you know?
就像，就像，它让我感到眩晕，你知道吗？

00:06:26.639 --> 00:06:28.279
I always forget that.
我总是忘记这一点。

00:06:28.279 --> 00:06:30.319
That's such a crazy detail.
这是一个非常疯狂的细节。

00:06:30.319 --> 00:06:32.319
Yeah, completely different energies.
是的，完全不同的能量。

00:06:32.319 --> 00:06:36.759
We were both butt-ass naked dicks, a swingin' in that play.
我们都是屁股赤裸的家伙，是那出戏中的摇摆人。

00:06:36.759 --> 00:06:37.600
For real.
真正的。

00:06:37.600 --> 00:06:38.439
How did I miss this one?
我怎么错过了这个？

00:06:38.439 --> 00:06:39.279
I remember being offstage.
我记得在台下。

00:06:39.279 --> 00:06:40.759
Did you get my text about heated rivalry?
你收到我关于激烈竞争的短信了吗？

00:06:40.759 --> 00:06:43.199
I said there'd be no heated rivalry without Paris letter.
我说过，如果没有巴黎信函，就不会有激烈的竞争。

00:06:43.199 --> 00:06:48.560
I love, I just did it to the rivalry.
我爱，我只是为了竞争才这么做的。

00:06:48.560 --> 00:06:51.120
It's good, can I add something?
很好，我可以添加一些东西吗？

00:06:51.120 --> 00:06:56.160
Your guys' specific chemistry and maybe what you just described was part of that.
你们的特殊化学反应，也许你刚才描述的就是其中的一部分。

00:06:57.240 --> 00:07:14.839
Whenever Ted and Barney went on an adventure together, sweet taste of liberty being a great example, or even just had a fucking scene together, there was some kind of energy that crackled between you guys and chemistry, and maybe a little bit of that slight disconnect were not, you guys had different assignments, you had different missions.
每当泰德和巴尼一起去冒险时，自由的甜蜜滋味就是一个很好的例子，或者甚至只是在一起他妈的场景，你们之间和化学反应之间就会产生某种能量，也许一点点轻微的脱节并不是，你们有不同的任务，有不同的任务。

00:07:14.839 --> 00:07:26.480
It was like the same, the same sort of overall mission, but within that you had very, very different roles, like an Oceans 11 kind of thing, like the safe crackers not exactly doing what the guys are climbing up the building is doing.
这就像相同的整体任务，但其中你有非常非常不同的角色，就像十一罗汉那样的事情，就像安全破解者不完全做那些爬上建筑物的人正在做的事情。

00:07:26.480 --> 00:07:37.040
And whatever that was, if there was a little bit of that, I think it added to the chemistry, whatever that mysterious thing is, why is Halli Met Your Mother still a show people talk about and care about?
不管那是什么，如果有一点点，我认为它增加了化学反应，不管那个神秘的东西是什么，为什么哈利遇见你的母亲仍然是一个人们谈论和关心的节目？

00:07:37.040 --> 00:07:38.639
Why are people still debating the finale?
为什么人们还在争论结局？

00:07:38.639 --> 00:07:39.879
Why are people still saying this?
为什么人们仍然这么说？

00:07:39.879 --> 00:07:47.160
There was just some mysterious energy to that thing, and it's bigger than any of us, but it is the combination of all of us.
那东西有一些神秘的能量，它比我们任何人都大，但它是我们所有人的结合体。

00:07:47.160 --> 00:07:52.279
And I think your guys specific combination as a duo was fantastic.
我认为你们作为二人组的特定组合非常棒。

00:07:52.279 --> 00:07:57.319
Even just in these first two seasons, watching YouTube and scenes and in storylines together, I love it.
即使只是在前两季，一起观看 YouTube、场景和故事情节，我也喜欢它。

00:07:57.319 --> 00:08:00.199
You are on weird little road trip movies, like Hope and Crosby.
你正在看一些奇怪的公路旅行小电影，比如《霍普》和《克罗斯比》。

00:08:00.199 --> 00:08:06.920
It's really interesting and those movies only work if those two people are very different and the energies are very different.
这真的很有趣，只有当这两个人非常不同并且能量非常不同时，这些电影才有效。

00:08:06.920 --> 00:08:09.079
That's a road trip movie and you guys had that.
那是一部公路旅行电影，你们已经看过了。

00:08:09.079 --> 00:08:16.399
You know also, Neil, I think that like, when you're, you know that thing we were just talking about, like the crew is like your only audience.
你也知道，尼尔，我认为，当你在的时候，你知道我们刚才谈论的事情，就像工作人员就像你唯一的观众一样。

00:08:16.399 --> 00:08:20.240
Like they laugh a lot when you do the run through and then it's diminishing returns.
就像当你进行运行时他们会大笑一样，然后收益递减。

00:08:20.240 --> 00:08:42.559
And I think when you're on a comedy, there's a kind of reflexive tendency to think, whoever's getting the most laughs is the most something valuable, or they're the, like the thing that I was doing and being asked to do, and I'm really delighted that I got some really good laughs on the show, but I was, like Craig is saying, my assignment was different.
我认为当你在喜剧中时，会有一种反射性的倾向，认为谁笑得最多就是最有价值的东西，或者他们就是，就像我正在做和被要求做的事情一样，我真的很高兴我在节目中得到了一些非常好的笑声，但我是，就像克雷格所说的那样，我的任务是不同的。

00:08:42.559 --> 00:08:47.879
And sometimes I felt like, is this valued the way that Neil's comedy is valued?
有时我想，这是否像尼尔的喜剧那样受到重视？

00:08:47.879 --> 00:08:51.080
Is my heart forward thing as valuable?
我的心向往的东西也同样有价值吗？

00:08:51.080 --> 00:08:57.639
And as the years have gone on, I realize, yes, all of the elements of the show made the show special and what it was.
随着时间的推移，我意识到，是的，这部剧的所有元素都让这部剧变得特别，它是什么。

00:08:57.639 --> 00:09:04.639
And so it took me a long time to realize that the task that I was given, I was doing it really well.
因此，我花了很长时间才意识到，我所承担的任务，我做得非常好。

00:09:04.639 --> 00:09:10.240
And I've actually gone back and kind of forgiven myself for being so hard on myself in those years, you know?
事实上，我已经回去并原谅了自己那些年对自己如此严厉，你知道吗？

00:09:10.240 --> 00:09:12.360
So that's why this rewatch has been really special.
这就是为什么这次重播非常特别。

00:09:12.360 --> 00:09:14.200
Yeah, I totally understand that.
是的，我完全理解这一点。

00:09:14.200 --> 00:09:23.000
Cause you would do an amazing, an amazingly executed speech about your heart and what it means.
因为你会发表一场令人惊叹的演讲，讲述你的内心及其意义。

00:09:23.000 --> 00:09:28.519
And then I would like spit up chicken and everyone would laugh at me.
然后我就想吐鸡，大家都会嘲笑我。

00:09:28.519 --> 00:09:29.360
Yeah.
是的。

00:09:29.360 --> 00:09:32.519
And then they'd say cut and then I'll be like, Neil, that was so funny.
然后他们会说剪掉，然后我就会说，尼尔，这太有趣了。

00:09:32.519 --> 00:09:35.120
The only thing is you hadn't even eaten chicken.
唯一的问题是你连鸡肉都没吃过。

00:09:35.120 --> 00:09:37.799
You just somehow, you're just that good.
你只是不知何故，你就是那么好。

00:09:37.799 --> 00:09:39.519
You just had chicken come out of you.
你刚刚从你身上生出了鸡肉。

00:09:39.519 --> 00:09:40.360
No, it's true.
不，这是真的。

00:09:40.360 --> 00:09:41.679
It's true.
这是真的。

00:09:41.679 --> 00:09:45.799
There was a longer tale for my kind of what I was offering.
对于我所提供的东西，还有一个更长的故事。

00:09:45.799 --> 00:10:01.120
And, but yeah, I mean, I know that without you playing Barney, we don't have a nine year run, you know, like not just cause you were so great to the execs, but like you were just not your powerful mighty force on this show.
而且，但是，是的，我的意思是，我知道如果没有你扮演巴尼，我们就不会连续九年，你知道，不仅因为你对高管如此出色，而且因为你在这部剧中并不是你强大的力量。

00:10:01.120 --> 00:10:06.639
And I think you gave like an all-timer performance, like a totally classic performance.
我认为你的表演就像一场空前的表演，一场完全经典的表演。

